{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/360960-the-spirit-world-and-dead-werewolves","id":360960,"title":"The spirit world and dead werewolves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-05T21:57:41-08:00","id":360960,"title":"The spirit world and dead werewolves","content":"I just ran a game where the PC's killed a few werewolves in the spirit world. I was wondering what happens to their corpses while in the spirit world. Do they decay away as they would in the physical world or do they dissipate like a spirit would?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3137-spiritsponge","name":"SpiritSponge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-05T22:40:30-08:00","id":360997,"title":"","content":"I think the corpses remain around, and if so, my headcanon is that they'd leave a mark on the land. You'd come across this vaguely swirling mess that looks like a skeleton, attended to by spirits of death, decay and battle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T01:16:45-08:00","id":361078,"title":"","content":"I picture lots of spirits tearing apart the corpse for essence pretty soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T05:23:27-08:00","id":361154,"title":"","content":"I don't know if there's any specific rules for it but I tend to treat corpses as nice piles of essence with resonance based on who the person was before they died and how they died.<br /> <br /> This was taken advantage of in one story where some werewolves killed an occultist and stashed his corpse in the Shadow of a graveyard. It was gobbled up by some more natural death and decay spirits and became a magath known as the Ghoul, which went around eating corpses, hating werewolves (influenced by its death at their hands, though it wasn't aware of this), and feeding its thirst for more power by becoming the top spirit of the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}